Third-party components and interoperability notes
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

mcbench does not bundle, vendor, or redistribute any of the following. They are
resolved, downloaded, or invoked at runtime on the operator's own machine. This
list records the licence boundaries that shaped mcbench's architecture; see
docs/LICENSING.md for the full analysis.

Minecraft: Java Edition — Mojang AB / Microsoft
    Proprietary. Not redistributed. Provisioned at runtime through official
    channels using the operator's own licensed account.
    https://www.minecraft.net/en-us/eula

Mods under test — respective authors
    Not redistributed. Resolved and downloaded at runtime from Modrinth (and
    optionally CurseForge, with an operator-supplied API key), honouring each
    author's distribution settings.

HeadlessMC — MIT License
    Invoked as an external process for headless client provisioning.
    https://github.com/3arthqu4ke/headlessmc

fabric-carpet — MIT License
    Optionally loaded at runtime; its tick-warp command is used as a
    deterministic server-side workload driver.
    https://github.com/gnembon/fabric-carpet

packwiz — MIT License
    Its TOML modpack metadata format inspired mcbench's mod-set declarations.
    https://github.com/packwiz/packwiz

spark — GNU GPLv3 (core), MIT (spark-api submodule only)
    NOT linked. mcbench never compiles or links against spark's GPLv3 core.
    Where spark is present in an operator's instance, mcbench interoperates
    only through loose runtime boundaries. See docs/LICENSING.md § spark.
    https://github.com/lucko/spark
